\s1 Nebuchadnezzar’s Troubling Dream
\p \v 1 \w In the second|strong="H8147"\w* \w year|strong="H8141"\w* \w of his|strong="H5019"\w* \w reign|strong="H4438"\w*, \w Nebuchadnezzar|strong="H5019"\w* \w had dreams|strong="H2492"\w* \w that troubled|strong="H6470"\w* \w his spirit|strong="H7307"\w*, \w and sleep|strong="H8142"\w* \w escaped|strong="H1961"\w* \w him|strong="H5921"\w*. \v 2 \w So the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w gave orders|strong="H559"\w* \w to summon|strong="H7121"\w* \w the magicians|strong="H825"\w*, \w enchanters|strong="H2748"\w*, \w sorcerers|strong="H3784"\w*, \w and astrologers|strong="H3778"\w*\f + \fr 2:2 \ft Or \fqa Chaldeans\ft ; also in verses 4, 5, and 10\f* \w to explain|strong="H5046"\w* \w his dreams|strong="H2472"\w*. \w When they came|strong="H935"\w* \w and stood|strong="H5975"\w* \w before|strong="H6440"\w* \w the king|strong="H4428"\w*, \v 3 \w he|strong="H4428"\w* \w said to them|strong="H559"\w*, “\w I have had a dream|strong="H2472"\w*, \w and my spirit|strong="H7307"\w* \w is anxious|strong="H6470"\w* \w to understand|strong="H3045"\w* \w it|strong="H2472"\w*.”
